      "Processors and backups are where lifecycle projects stall. If the fiduciary must erase, the processor must erase too. A backup that restores the deleted file next Tuesday has not really erased it. A recommendation is to know how backups age out, and to write that into the vendor contract before 13 May 2027. You do not need to pretend the contract clause is already a statutory breach if it is missing on 2 October 2026. You do need a plan. An insurer, for example, can ask its cloud vendor how a deleted policyholder phone number leaves active systems and backups, and can record the answer as preparation rather than as a completed section 8 audit.",
