      "A consent banner is a screen. A Consent Manager is a legal person with a registration. Section 2 defines that person as someone registered with the Board, a single point of contact for giving, managing, reviewing, and withdrawing consent on an accessible, transparent, and interoperable platform. Your own banner, however polished, is the Data Fiduciary talking to its own user. It is not that registered person. Section 6(9) registration commences on 13 November 2026, with section 27(1)(d) and Rule 4. On 2 October 2026 it is not in force. If a launch plan says 'we go live as a Consent Manager on Friday,' stop the plan.",
