      "Do not add a fake ground to the banner. A toggle labelled legitimate interest is a GDPR control, not a DPDP one. If you are relying on a certain legitimate use, such as the address the customer just typed for the delivery she asked for, you do not need to dress that use up as a foreign balancing test. If you want a separate festival promotion, ask for specific consent. Pre-ticked boxes are not a clear affirmative action. A jewellery site that pre-ticks 'share with partners' is the scene to unpick. Section 7 and section 6 commence on 13 May 2027. Until then, a clean banner is a recommendation, not a commenced defence.",
