      "Role mapping is the second page. Who decides the purpose? That organisation is the Data Fiduciary. Who only hosts or sends on instruction? That organisation is the Data Processor. If a vendor wants the data for its own model, give that flow a fiduciary label of its own. Do not add a third crown called Significant Data Fiduciary unless a Central Government notification under section 10 exists. Do not add a fourth crown called Consent Manager unless someone is actually registered, which cannot have happened yet on the review date. A manufacturer, for example, may be fiduciary for dealer contacts and processor for a brand principal's warranty file. The map should show both. Section 10 commences on 13 May 2027. Registration commences on 13 November 2026.",
      "Grounds and notices are the third page. For each purpose, write consent or the section 7 use, in the Act's words, not 'legitimate interest.' Draft the notice with data, purpose, rights, and the complaint path. Plan a clear affirmative action and a withdrawal that is as easy as the yes. Keep the record you will need when the burden of proof in section 6 commences. A bank can separate 'send this account alert' from 'send a partner's credit-card offer.' The alert may sit close to the service. The offer needs its own consent design. Sections 4, 5, 6, and 7 commence on 13 May 2027. The drafts are preparation. They are not a declaration that enforcement has begun.",
      "Children, rights, and contacts are the customer-facing half. Use eighteen as the age. Plan verifiable parent or guardian consent and do not build tracking ads aimed at children. Sketch access, correction, erasure, grievance, and nomination, and leave prescribed timelines blank rather than inventing them. Name a person who can answer. If you are not a notified SDF, that person is your contact under the future section 8 duty, not a section 10 Data Protection Officer. A gaming company can put these four items on one roadmap and date section 9 and sections 11 to 14 to 13 May 2027. The roadmap should also say the children's penalty maximum is up to Rs 200 crore, not automatic, and not in force on the review date.",
      "Security and incidents are where programmes either protect people or perform paperwork. Choose safeguards that match the data: access control, protection of stored identity files, and a check on who your processor lets in. Those examples are recommendations, not a statutory shopping list. Write the incident card in the words of section 8: tell the Board and each affected Data Principal, in the form and manner prescribed, when the duty is in force. Cross out 72 hours if it appears as a DPDP rule. A hospital group can run a tabletop that stops at 'draft the explanation' and does not pretend a filing is legally due today. The safeguard maximum of up to Rs 250 crore and the notification maximum of up to Rs 200 crore commence on 13 May 2027.",
      "Vendors, retention, and transfers keep the programme from living only in the privacy team's folder. Every processor needs a contract path before section 8 commences: purpose, safeguards, help on an incident, and deletion. The retention schedule cites a real law or an internal rule, never a made-up statutory year. The transfer map has a blank column for a section 16 restriction notification, because the Act is not a whitelist and not a general ban. A retailer can review its top ten vendors against those three pages in a month. Mark the work preparation. A missing clause on 2 October 2026 is a gap to close, not a commenced penalty. Say that in the procurement minutes so the commercial team is not misled.",
      "Governance and training stop the programme rotting. Name an owner. Meet often enough to look at new products. Teach support staff the duties in section 15 without turning Rs 10,000 into a threat, and teach them that rights are not yet enforceable. Teach product staff that Consent Guru is a tool, not a registered Consent Manager and not the Board. A quarterly hour for a 300-person firm can cover one module's mistakes, such as a pre-ticked box or an SDF claim in a press note. The training deck's first line should repeat the review date and the two future dates. If the deck is titled 'we are already certified,' change the title. This course does not certify anyone.",
      "Sequence the last page like a calendar, not a wish. From now until 13 November 2026, build the machinery and do not claim Consent Manager registration. On and after that date, registration is a specific legal step for a person who will be a Consent Manager, not a sticker for a banner. From now until 13 May 2027, finish the operational artefacts, knowing they are preparation. On that date, sections 3 to 17, most Board enforcement, appeals, and penalties are appointed to commence. For example, put those sentences in the board pack instead of a red-amber-green that hides the gazette. This module is education. It is not legal advice that your programme is sufficient.",
