      "This last module leaves the classroom and walks into five ordinary organisations. Keep the calendar in your pocket. Today, for this course, is 2 October 2026. Section 2 and the Board's institutional provisions have been in force since 13 November 2025. Consent Manager registration starts on 13 November 2026 and has not started. The duties that change forms, ads, security programmes, and breach letters start on 13 May 2027. A founder who wants a single word, 'live' or 'not live,' is asking the wrong question. Say which section. Then apply it to the scene in front of you. The scenes are education, not a ruling on a real company.",
      "Take a food-delivery app. It decides why it collects a phone number and an address, so it is the Data Fiduciary. The cloud company that only hosts the database is a processor. Using the address to deliver the meal the customer ordered is the kind of voluntary provision section 7 describes, if she has not indicated that she does not consent to that use. A separate 'offers from restaurants you have never heard of' programme is a consent design, not a legitimate-interest checkbox. The app's banner is not a Consent Manager, and Consent Guru, if they use it, is not one either. If a seventeen-year-old can open an account, the children's rules in section 9 are on the future build list. None of those operational duties is being enforced today.",
